  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Future is in the Backlands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smallholder producers in the semi-arid lowland region of Gran Chaco lack consistent income-generating opportunities. Fundacin Gran Chaco (FGCH) provides technical assistance that enables Indigenous and criollo producers to develop their entities as organizations, gain access to more markets and improve their crafts, processed foods, and forest products. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions to expand economic opportunity in Latin America and the Caribbean. FGCH&apos;s activities promote smallholder agriculture and food production to ensure meaningful opportunities for communities to thrive. FY24 Amendment: This amendment provides FGCH with an additional two years and $125,900 to strengthen its management and communications capacity, share best practices, and document learning for a grassroots network of more than 90 Indigenous and Creole communities in the Gran Chaco region of Argentina. FGCH will develop its Saberes del Monte management system that will provide tools for grassroots users to help strengthen the administrative, financial, outreach, and fundraising skills of each organization. As part of the amendment, FGCH is mobilizing an additional $158,200 in counterpart resources to the grant agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
